  <running_head>COMMENT. IN IOSVE</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Hæc</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">bes iftę &amp; villę earum.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">40 Tribui filiorum Dan per fami-</l>
    <l n="3">lias suas exiuit sors septima.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">41 Fuítque terminus hæreditatis eo-</l>
    <l n="5">rum, Sorah, &amp; Esthaol, &amp; Itsemes,</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">42 Et Saalabbin, &amp; Aialon, &amp; Ith-</l>
    <l n="7">lah.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">43 Et Elon, &amp; Thimnathah, &amp; Ekron,</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">44 Et Elthece, &amp; Gibbethon, &amp;</l>
    <l n="10">Baalath,</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">45 Et Iehud, &amp; Bene-berac, &amp;</l>
    <l n="12">Gath-rimon,</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">46 Et Mehaiarcon, &amp; Raccon cum</l>
    <l n="14">termino contra Iapho.</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">47 Et exiuit terminus filiorum</l>
    <l n="16">Dan ab eis: ascenderuntque filii Dan, &amp;</l>
    <l n="17">pugnauerunt cum Lesem, ceperúnt-</l>
    <l n="18">que eam, ac percusserūt eam acie gla-</l>
    <l n="19">dii, &amp; hæreditate acceperunt eam, ha-</l>
    <l n="20">bitauerúntque in ea: &amp; vocauerūt Le-</l>
    <l n="21">sem Dan secundum nomen Dan pa-</l>
    <l n="22">tris sui.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">48 Hæc</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword "Hæc" at lower right, which also begins the next verse; the line "48 Hæc" is printed at right and is kept as the catchword. Some words are uncertain in the scan, including the Latin spelling of "ascenderunt" (printed "afcéderúntque") and the Hebrew place names, which were read as printed.</notes>
